	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(-130, -60, 420, 50)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Lab 5: Classification of Images**  
Cats and dogs, 24 pictures of each</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/markdown" rect="(-130, 800, 230, 90)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 2: Training images**  
Reads classificationDataset/train (12 cats, 12 dogs).</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/markdown" rect="(120, 70, 250, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Steps 2-3: SqueezeNet**  
Turns each picture into 1000 numbers. The Data Table shows them.</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/markdown" rect="(800, 20, 300, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 4: Models**  
Five models with their default settings, scored with 10-fold cross-validation.</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/markdown" rect="(1180, 180, 230, 90)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 5: Confusion matrix**  
Right and wrong guesses for each model.</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/markdown" rect="(60, 1250, 300, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 6: Best embedder**  
Inception v3 gave the highest accuracy in my experiments, so this part uses it.</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/markdown" rect="(1000, 1250, 330, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 7: Test on test data**  
Models trained on the training pictures and scored on the test pictures.</text>
		<text id="7" type="text/markdown" rect="(160, 1760, 430, 90)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 7: Test images**  
Reads classificationDataset/test (12 cats, 12 dogs). Same embedder as the training data.</text>
		<text id="8" type="text/markdown" rect="(45, 440, 150, 30)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Training data**</text>
		<text id="9" type="text/markdown" rect="(790, 1400, 110, 30)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Test data**</text>
		<arrow id="10" start="(0, 800)" end="(45, 750)" fill="#C1272D" />
